            <ArticleTitle>Evaluating the effectiveness of Tegapore wound-contact material.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During wound healing, new-forming granulation tissue is often extremely fragile and can be easily disrupted during dressing changes. This can lead to a delay in the completion of wound healing and increased pain and discomfort for the patient (European Wound Management Association, 2002; Fear, 2002).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
